TITLE:: Range Symbols
summary:: Guidelines for writing range symbols.
categories:: MusicEngine Library
related:: Classes/MENoteRange, Classes/MERange, Classes/MENote, Classes/MERegister

DESCRIPTION::
This document is a reference of how to write range symbols using the verbose syntax, as well as providing a listing of all aliases allowed in STRONG::MusicEngine::.

SECTION:: Verbose Syntax

Range may be described by:
LIST::
## Referencing the root note (capital EMPHASIS::A-G::), with or without STRONG::zero:: to STRONG::five:: accidentals (#/b)
## using a letter to describe interval quality (EMPHASIS::d, m, P, M, A::) and
## using a number to represent the degree (EMPHASIS::1-14::)
::

SUBSECTION:: Allowed intervals
Depending on the degree, an interval may be EMPHASIS::diminished::, EMPHASIS::minor::, EMPHASIS::perfect::, EMPHASIS::major:: or EMPHASIS::augmented::. Represented, respectively, by EMPHASIS::d, m, P, M, A::.

TABLE::
## STRONG::Degree:: || STRONG::Type::
## 1st || A
## 8th || d, A
## 2nd/9th || m, M, A
## 7th/14th || d, m, M
## 3rd/10th; 6th/13th || d, m, M, A
## 4th/11th; 5th/12th || d, P, A
::

SUBSECTION:: Rules

LIST::
## Number of intervals may range from STRONG::two:: to STRONG::eleven::, not counting the root (EMPHASIS::P1::). With two being a single interval, and eleven a chromatic scale.

CODE::
a = MENoteRange.new("F#P5");                     // Perfect five over F#
b = MENoteRange.new("F#m2M2m3M3P4A4P5m6M6m7M7"); // Chromatic scale over F#
::

## Enharmonic intervals are not allowed (e.g.: EMPHASIS::A2/m3::, EMPHASIS::m3/A9::, EMPHASIS::A4/d5::, etc.).

CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#m3P5M7A9"); // ERROR: 0, 3, 3, 7, 11 contains enharmonics.
// P1 = 0, A9 = 3, m3 = 3, P5 = 7, M7 = 11
::

## Diminished seconds and augmented sevents are not allowed, since they're enharmonic to the root.
CODE::
r = MENoteRange.new("F#m3P5A7");   // ERROR: A7, Is not a valid interval.
r = MENoteRange.new("F#m3P5M7d9"); // ERROR: d9, Is not a valid interval.
::

## Any root note is allowed, provided there are only 0 to 3 accidentals.
CODE::
a = MENoteRange.new("F-7");
b = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
c = MENoteRange.new("F##-7");
d = MENoteRange.new("F###-7");
e = MENoteRange.new("F####-7"); // ERROR: F####, is not a valid root.
::

## Duplicated intervals are not allowed, since they're a form of enharmonics.
CODE::
a = MENoteRange.new("F#m3P5m3m7");  // ERROR: m3 is duplicate. Intervals must be unique.
::

## Intervals may be in any order since they're sorted internally by their numeric representation (EMPHASIS::m3P5m7M9:: = EMPHASIS::3.1, 5.2, 7.1, 9.3::).
CODE::
a = MENoteRange.new("F#m7m3M9P5");

// Yields the exact same result as:
b = MENoteRange.new("F#m3P5m7M9");

a == b; // true
::
::

SECTION:: Aliases
The alias system provides a more convenient way of specifying conventional symbols. When generating a range, the user may use, either, the alias, or its verbose equivalent:

CODE::
a = MENoteRange.new("F#m3P5m7");
// Same as:
b = MENoteRange.new("F#-7");
a == b; // true
::

As such, the following aliases are allowed:

SUBSECTION:: Chord aliases

SUBSUBSECTION:: Power chords

TABLE::
## STRONG::Description:: || STRONG::Alias:: || STRONG::Verbose syntax::
## Perfect fifth || 5 || P5
::

SUBSUBSECTION:: Triads

TABLE::
## STRONG::Description:: || STRONG::Alias:: || STRONG::Verbose syntax::
## Diminished triad || Dim, dim, Dim5, dim5, o5, 05, o, 0 || m3d5
## Minor triad 	    || m, Mi, mi, Min, min, - || m3P5
## Major triad 	    || ""FOOTNOTE::A root note without any symbol (e.g. EMPHASIS::C, F#, Bb,:: etc.) defaultas to the major triad.::, M, Ma, ma, Maj, maj, ^, Neapolitan, neapolitan, Nap, nap, Na, na || M3P5
## Augmented triad  || Aug, aug, Aug5, aug5, +5, + 	|| M3A5
::

SUBSUBSECTION:: Seventh chords

TABLE::
## STRONG::Description:: || STRONG::Alias:: || STRONG::Verbose syntax::
## Diminished seventh    || Dim7, dim7, o7, 07 || m3d5d7
## Half-diminished seventh || m7o5, m705, Mi7o5, Mi705, mi7o5, mi705, Min7o5, Min705, min7o5, min705, -7o5, -705 || m3d5m7
## Minor seventh || Mi7, mi7, Min7, min7, -7 || m3P5m7
## Minor-major seventh || mM, mM7, MiMa7, mima7, MinMaj7, minmaj7, m^7, Mi^7, mi^7, Min^7, min^7, -^7 || m3P5M7
## Dominant seventh || Dom, dom, Dom7, dom7, 7 || M3P5m7
## Major seventh || Ma7, ma7, Maj7, maj7, ^7 || M3P5M7
::

